    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "57b5fa86-9964-5965-a96f-e7e4ac215d5d",
      ":question/problem": "![](/tmp/course-academy-g2-readonly-tly0pcma/17592186096649/caller-easy/generated/c0b88123a7c2d372c2150fb51ccc590b950e3c790c0452d1e892fce79efc1695.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the vector $\\mathbf{a}$. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $-\\mathbf{a}$?",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that $-\\mathbf{a}$ must be parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nNow, for the vector $-\\mathbf{a}$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $-\\mathbf{a}$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $-\\mathbf{a}$ have opposite directions since the factor $-1$ is negative.\n\nThe required vectors are shown below.\n\n![](/tmp/course-academy-g2-readonly-tly0pcma/17592186096649/caller-easy/generated/578c24a7532fddcb62bed77567e4dd28fa40eb1ee7e1933dbe1c48e8284e504d.png)",
