      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that $-2\\mathbf{a}$ must be parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nNow, for the vector $-2\\mathbf{a}$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $-2\\mathbf{a}$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $-2\\mathbf{a}$ have opposite directions since the factor $-2$ is negative.\n\nThe required vectors are shown below.\n\n![](/tmp/course-academy-g2-readonly-tly0pcma/17592186096649/caller-easy/generated/b5e7bae1c7832c93345f0de77dfb18dc2c5b4c9f11dbbf678c5712935da0a804.png)",
